# Sample data artifacts
*.csv
*.json
*.bpmn
*.zip
# BPS models are the experimental apparatus, not build output: the blanket
# *.json / *.bpmn rules above would otherwise leave every model a paper's
# results depend on untracked, while tracking the .csv.gz logs that go with
# them -- a clone would get the logs and not the models, and the evaluation
# pipelines would not run. Generator scripts live in tools/generate_*.py, but
# they are unseeded, so re-running them does NOT reproduce these exact files.
!samples/**/*.bpmn
!samples/**/*.json

# The experiment records the harness's numbers are cited from. They stay in the
# repository even though the paper sources do not, so the blanket *.csv rule
# above must not swallow the results table the records refer to.
!docs/state-metrics/*.csv

# Paper sources: LaTeX, the figure PDFs and the data the figure scripts read.
# Drafted outside this repository; the durable record is docs/state-metrics/.
/paper/

# Loose working files at the root -- run logs, half-finished notes, one-off
# scripts. Anything worth keeping goes to docs/state-metrics/ under a real name.
/scratch_*
/.codex

!package.json
!package-lock.json
!tsconfig.json
!pyproject.toml
